---
import { links } from "../content/site";
import FeatureTile from "../ui/FeatureTile.astro";
import SectionHead from "../ui/SectionHead.astro";
import ChatView from "../views/chat/ChatView.astro";
import McpView from "../views/mcp/McpView.astro";
import PromptsView from "../views/prompts/PromptsView.astro";
import ActionsView from "../views/actions/ActionsView.astro";
import "./Features.css";
---

<section id="features" class="section features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <div class="wrap-wide">
    <SectionHead eyebrow="Features" id="features-title">
      <Fragment slot="title"
        >Plan in a chat, control every prompt, and run your commands in the worktree.</Fragment
      >
      <p>
        Chats and the MCP server use the same local task store as the board. A task that an agent
        creates in a chat or through MCP shows on the board at once.
      </p>
    </SectionHead>
    <div class="features-grid">
      <FeatureTile
        id="feature-chat"
        label="Chats"
        title="Plan a feature in a chat, and get tasks on the board."
        size="full"
      >
        A chat works outside a task. Give it a custom role and a reusable prompt. The agent searches
        your tasks and creates the missing ones. Open a new task from the chat, and start its
        Builder without leaving the chat.
        <ChatView slot="view" />
      </FeatureTile>
      <FeatureTile
        id="feature-mcp"
        label="MCP"
        title="Use your tasks from any MCP client."
        size="half"
      >
        Add <a class="text-link" href={links.mcp}><code>@openducktor/mcp</code></a> to another agent.
        It can search, read, create, and update your tasks. It sends each call to the running app, so
        the board shows a new task at once.
        <McpView slot="view" />
      </FeatureTile>
      <FeatureTile
        id="feature-prompts"
        label="Prompts"
        title="Read and replace every built-in prompt."
        size="half"
      >
        The settings show each built-in prompt that OpenDucktor sends to an agent. Replace a prompt
        for all repositories or for one repository. OpenDucktor checks the placeholders of each
        active override, and it does not save until they are valid.
        <PromptsView slot="view" />
      </FeatureTile>
      <FeatureTile
        id="feature-actions"
        label="Actions"
        title="Run your project commands in the task worktree."
        size="full"
      >
        An action is a named command of the repository, such as your dev server or your tests. Run
        it from the top bar of a session: each run opens a new terminal in the worktree of the task,
        or in the folder of the chat. An action can also run when OpenDucktor creates a worktree,
        and the agent can wait until it finishes.
        <ActionsView slot="view" />
      </FeatureTile>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
